{
  "about": "The causes the registry walk reaches through one core entry point each, with no specification: an application's refusals (OUTPUT-8, FUNC-3 and the engine's own), a resource path that an input or a save target refuses (FILE-5, FILE-7, FILE-8, FILE-10), numeric evaluation (FORMULA-9, FORMULA-12, FORMULA-15, VALUE-5), value conversion (VALUE-3, VALUE-7, VALUE-15), the column checks of a verification (CHECK-5 to CHECK-9, SUB-11, SUB-13, SUB-26, CT-7), an invalid pattern (TEXT-6), rounding (FORMULA-16) and the extremes of sources that cannot be compared (VALUE-19). A numeric evaluation that fails names the failed node by its bytes in the expression, past any group around it, and by the operand steps that reach it; numeric text that VALUE-6 does not admit fails conversion to `int` and to `float` alike. A case whose walk compared a record in part names those fields, or those keys of its context, in compares.",
